<title>USA: Northland Cranberries completes purchase.</title>
<headline>Northland Cranberries completes purchase.</headline>
<dateline>WISCONSIN RAPIDS, Wis. 1996-12-30</dateline>
<text>
<p>Northland Cranberries Inc said Monday it completed its acquisition of a 798-acre cranberry property in central Wisconsin from Vanatta Cranberry Co LLC.</p>
<p>The purchase price was $4.35 million, including $2.175 million in cash and 100,000 shares of Northland class A common stock, the company said.</p>
<p>The 798-acre acquisition includes 73 acres of planted cranberry vines, buildings and all related operating assets.</p>
<p>Northland said total planted acreage for the company is now about 2,589 with more than 23,000 acres of additional support land.</p>
<p>((--Chicago newsdesk, 312-408-8787))</p>
